  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Asia Water Governance Programme (SAWGP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To improve the management of water within and between South Asian countries, reducing poverty by enabling adaptation to climate change and reducing the risk of conflict over water resources. By 2018, 500 million people living in river basins will benefit from improved water management by reducing their risk of exposure to flooding and drought and enhancing regional security by improving cooperation between governments</narrative>
  </description>
